WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.669
-Our next guest
is an iconic illusionist

00:00:02.669 --> 00:00:06.305
who has won 21 Emmys, earned
11 Guinness World Records,

00:00:06.305 --> 00:00:08.608
and has been named
a living legend

00:00:08.608 --> 00:00:10.510
by the US Library of Congress.

00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:13.846
His book, "David Copperfield's
History of Magic,"

00:00:13.846 --> 00:00:15.047
is available now.

00:00:15.047 --> 00:00:17.750
Get your copy...
before it disappears.

00:00:17.750 --> 00:00:18.918
Please welcome to the show

00:00:18.918 --> 00:00:21.621
the always great
David Copperfield!

00:00:21.621 --> 00:00:23.456
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:23.456 --> 00:00:24.690
Hello, David.

00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:25.992
-How are you? How are you?

00:00:25.992 --> 00:00:28.428
-I'm doing very well.
I want to begin by asking --

00:00:28.428 --> 00:00:29.929
-I'm changing my name to Gaia,
by the way.

00:00:29.929 --> 00:00:31.464
I'm changing my name to Gaia.

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:33.465
-It's a very hot name right now.
Good.

00:00:33.465 --> 00:00:35.935
Getting in on the ground floor
is a good idea.

00:00:35.935 --> 00:00:37.470
What is the difference, David,

00:00:37.470 --> 00:00:41.473
between an illusionist
and a magician?

00:00:41.473 --> 00:00:44.144
-Well, my joke is, if you
call yourself an illusionist,

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:47.346
you get to make 20% more,
which is true.

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:50.249
-All right, so sort of like
a classy magician.

00:00:50.249 --> 00:00:52.685
-That's right.
-Now, I will speak to the fact

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:54.353
that I have seen your show live.

00:00:54.353 --> 00:00:56.389
Not only was it
incredibly memorable,

00:00:56.389 --> 00:00:58.091
even if it was made more so

00:00:58.091 --> 00:01:00.827
by the fact that I was there for
Andy Samberg's bachelor party,

00:01:00.827 --> 00:01:03.896
and then afterwards,
we went backstage,

00:01:03.896 --> 00:01:08.367
and you had
a very specific illusion

00:01:08.367 --> 00:01:10.236
built just for Andy.

00:01:10.236 --> 00:01:12.772
-I did. Well, what happened
was I was shocked

00:01:12.772 --> 00:01:14.206
that you guys were there
because, you know,

00:01:14.206 --> 00:01:15.474
bachelor party --

00:01:15.474 --> 00:01:18.410
you have strippers
or David Copperfield?

00:01:18.410 --> 00:01:21.814
"Hmm. Okay.
David Copperfield. Perfect."

00:01:21.814 --> 00:01:24.149
So, I'm doing the show,
and backstage,

00:01:24.149 --> 00:01:29.622
my whole crew is building
a "dick in the box" box

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:31.524
because Andy was there.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:32.959
And, you know,
they're crafting it.

00:01:32.959 --> 00:01:34.827
The glue is drying,
and the show's over with.

00:01:34.827 --> 00:01:36.295
And I come backstage.

00:01:36.295 --> 00:01:38.465
You were very kind to come
backstage and say hello.

00:01:38.465 --> 00:01:41.500
And we levitated a box
with my magic.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:44.370
Here is a floating
dick in the box.

00:01:44.370 --> 00:01:48.474
[ Laughter ]

00:01:48.474 --> 00:01:50.843
Fantastic.
-Yes.

00:01:50.843 --> 00:01:55.248
-So, you have -- Over the years,
you've basically built

00:01:55.248 --> 00:01:56.415
a museum of magic.

00:01:56.415 --> 00:01:57.884
You are in it right now.

00:01:57.884 --> 00:02:00.052
It is your sort of
self-curated museum.

00:02:00.052 --> 00:02:01.787
It is not open to the public.

00:02:01.787 --> 00:02:03.756
One of the reasons is
there are so many secrets

00:02:03.756 --> 00:02:05.658
that would be revealed
if people saw it.

00:02:05.658 --> 00:02:07.293
So now you've put together
this book,

00:02:07.293 --> 00:02:09.828
which is sort of a peek inside.

00:02:09.828 --> 00:02:12.564
Was it fun to sort of
pick out your favorite pieces

00:02:12.564 --> 00:02:14.433
and tell the backstory of them?

00:02:14.433 --> 00:02:16.535
-It was awesome because
there's so many amazing stories

00:02:16.535 --> 00:02:20.239
of the ladies and gentlemen
who inform this art form,

00:02:20.239 --> 00:02:21.674
and the art form of magic

00:02:21.674 --> 00:02:24.878
really has influenced art,
influenced design,

00:02:24.878 --> 00:02:28.448
influenced robotics, technology.

00:02:28.448 --> 00:02:30.116
Incredible things.

00:02:30.116 --> 00:02:32.652
The first smart home to exist
was a magic effect.

00:02:32.652 --> 00:02:34.220
Robert-Houdin.

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:36.288
His actual house door
is behind me there.

00:02:36.288 --> 00:02:39.225
It's a door that opens up,
you know, by magic.

00:02:39.225 --> 00:02:41.493
And now every grocery store,
you know --

00:02:41.493 --> 00:02:44.029
Every CVS we go to
to get the shot,

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:45.197
you go through that --

00:02:45.197 --> 00:02:46.598
That was a trick at the time.

00:02:46.598 --> 00:02:49.502
So all kinds of things
were affected by magic,

00:02:49.502 --> 00:02:53.005
and I get to tell those stories
in a really wonderful way.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.374
At this museum, you know,
we've had, you know --

00:02:55.374 --> 00:02:58.310
Guillermo del Toro will be here,
and he'll get very emotional

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:02.514
because the cinema was invented
as a magic effect.

00:03:02.514 --> 00:03:04.317
Movies was a magic trick.

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:08.020
And Georges Méliès
took that magic effect

00:03:08.020 --> 00:03:11.391
and made it into something
that we could tell stories with.

00:03:11.391 --> 00:03:13.959
So much of what we live
in our life

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.562
has been prototyped
by magicians.

00:03:16.562 --> 00:03:18.998
-Do you remember
the first trick you did?

00:03:18.998 --> 00:03:22.535
Was magic something that had
come to you at a very young age?

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.170
-I made my teacher disappear.

00:03:24.170 --> 00:03:25.738
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.738 --> 00:03:27.339
I was very popular.

00:03:27.339 --> 00:03:32.145
But then she came back, and
all my street cred was lost.

00:03:32.145 --> 00:03:33.946
-You, uh --

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:37.383
This is a true story that seems
like it shouldn't be.

00:03:37.383 --> 00:03:40.953
The secrets to your tricks
are hidden somewhere

00:03:40.953 --> 00:03:43.389
so that whenever you are gone,

00:03:43.389 --> 00:03:45.958
people could look
and read your secrets.

00:03:45.958 --> 00:03:48.360
Where have you hidden
the secrets to your tricks?

00:03:48.360 --> 00:03:50.463
-On the Moon.

00:03:50.463 --> 00:03:52.565
-"On the Moon" is a real answer.

00:03:52.565 --> 00:03:55.301
How did you get them
to the Moon?

00:03:55.301 --> 00:03:57.737
-Well, what happened was
we're able to put them

00:03:57.737 --> 00:03:59.272
on nickel discs.

00:03:59.272 --> 00:04:01.240
The Arch Mission, my friends
at the Arch Mission,

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.943
were able to etch my secrets
into a nickel disc.

00:04:03.943 --> 00:04:07.079
And nickel doesn't degrade.
That element doesn't degrade.

00:04:07.079 --> 00:04:08.881
It'll be there
for a billion years.

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:10.616
And those disc
with all my secrets

00:04:10.616 --> 00:04:14.220
were sent to the Moon
in an Israeli lander.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.722
Unfortunately,
it didn't land nice.

00:04:16.722 --> 00:04:19.225
It landed -- It crash-landed.

00:04:19.225 --> 00:04:21.427
But the things don't --

00:04:21.427 --> 00:04:22.996
They still exist there
on the Moon.

00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:24.863
They're a little harder to find.

00:04:24.863 --> 00:04:27.566
But someday,
if you are on the Moon

00:04:27.566 --> 00:04:30.836
and you have a metal detector
and a microscope,

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:32.571
you can actually see my magic.

00:04:32.571 --> 00:04:34.107
In fact,
we're going to try again

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.741
with those secrets and the book.

00:04:35.741 --> 00:04:37.476
So the book and my secrets
are going to the Moon.

00:04:37.476 --> 00:04:40.246
So if you don't buy the book,
someday you can go to the Moon

00:04:40.246 --> 00:04:42.247
and actually read the book
on the Moon.

00:04:42.247 --> 00:04:44.883
-Are you worried that if
an alien race ever found

00:04:44.883 --> 00:04:50.556
that first, they'd think Earth
was just a planet of magicians?

00:04:50.556 --> 00:04:52.458
-[ Laughs ] That's true.
And it would kill my career.

00:04:52.458 --> 00:04:54.060
[ Laughter ]

00:04:54.060 --> 00:04:56.562
-Is it true that you were
once held up at gunpoint

00:04:56.562 --> 00:04:59.265
and did a trick
to get out of it?

00:04:59.265 --> 00:05:00.900
-Yeah, that was
a pretty stupid day.

00:05:00.900 --> 00:05:03.102
I was held up at gunpoint
with my crew, in fact.

00:05:03.102 --> 00:05:04.570
About six of us were there.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:07.072
They held a gun to our faces,

00:05:07.072 --> 00:05:08.941
and everybody
gave their passports

00:05:08.941 --> 00:05:10.743
and their money, smartly.

00:05:10.743 --> 00:05:13.145
I, stupidly, just by instinct,

00:05:13.145 --> 00:05:15.314
did what magicians call
a pocket dodge,

00:05:15.314 --> 00:05:18.484
which is where you could show
your pockets empty

00:05:18.484 --> 00:05:20.452
and they're not really empty.

00:05:20.452 --> 00:05:23.889
And, you know, I didn't
want to give up my passport

00:05:23.889 --> 00:05:26.726
and my money, and I should have,
but it worked out okay.

00:05:26.726 --> 00:05:28.727
The criminals were caught, and
I could've got my stuff back.

00:05:28.727 --> 00:05:30.730
But if you're out there
listening

00:05:30.730 --> 00:05:33.232
and you're able to do
the pocket-dodge effect,

00:05:33.232 --> 00:05:34.366
don't do it.

00:05:34.366 --> 00:05:35.902
Give them the money. It's okay.

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:39.605
-Now, obviously in that moment,
it must have been heartbreaking

00:05:39.605 --> 00:05:41.940
because you probably realized
they didn't recognize you

00:05:41.940 --> 00:05:44.610
as David Copperfield.
-[ Laughs ]

00:05:44.610 --> 00:05:46.412
-Because I'll tell you,
if I had a gun

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:48.380
and asked David Copperfield
to empty his pockets

00:05:48.380 --> 00:05:50.883
and he was like, "Nothing,"
I'd be like, "Hold on."

00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:52.685
[ Laughter ]

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:55.288
"I'm gonna check 'em myself,
Copperfield."

00:05:55.288 --> 00:05:58.057
-I probably did that move
because --

00:05:58.057 --> 00:06:00.860
I was really somebody,
you know, had some talent.

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:02.929
-This is very exciting.

00:06:02.929 --> 00:06:06.866
You actually not only have the
history of magic in your museum,

00:06:06.866 --> 00:06:10.168
you have a piece of history
from our show.

00:06:10.168 --> 00:06:11.970
We actually referenced him
tonight.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.308
You have the Sea Captain photo.

00:06:15.308 --> 00:06:17.009
[ Laughter ]

00:06:17.009 --> 00:06:19.312
-That's right. We've got
the Sea Captain from your house

00:06:19.312 --> 00:06:21.781
right here in 3-D.

00:06:21.781 --> 00:06:23.782
But he doesn't have a body.

00:06:23.782 --> 00:06:26.552
-What foul black magic is this?

00:06:26.552 --> 00:06:27.986
-He won't shut up.

00:06:27.986 --> 00:06:32.524
-May every fish you ever eat
have higher mercury levels!

00:06:32.524 --> 00:06:33.825
-I thought
I'd make him disappear.

00:06:33.825 --> 00:06:34.994
Is that okay with you?

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:37.596
-I won't go quietly,
Copperfield!

00:06:37.596 --> 00:06:39.398
You may banish me,

00:06:39.398 --> 00:06:42.635
but I will spend eternity
haunting your soul!

00:06:42.635 --> 00:06:44.737
And I can't find your soul,

00:06:44.737 --> 00:06:47.139
I'll take a ghost [bleep]
in your lawn!

00:06:47.139 --> 00:06:48.974
[ Cackling ]

00:06:48.974 --> 00:06:50.543
-Let's do this.

00:06:50.543 --> 00:06:54.347
-[Bleep] you, David Copperfield.

00:06:54.347 --> 00:06:55.981
N-o-o-o-o-o!

00:06:55.981 --> 00:06:57.349
Don't send me away.

00:06:57.349 --> 00:06:59.652
I promise I'll be good.

00:06:59.652 --> 00:07:00.853
[ Sobbing ]

00:07:00.853 --> 00:07:02.321
-He's still talking.

00:07:02.321 --> 00:07:05.524
-I will have my revenge,
Copperfield!

00:07:05.524 --> 00:07:08.294
-Oh, my God.
David, thank you so much

00:07:08.294 --> 00:07:11.263
for finally getting rid
of him for us.

00:07:11.263 --> 00:07:13.966
-[ Laughs ]
My pleasure. My pleasure.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.501
-David Copperfield, everybody.

00:07:15.501 --> 00:07:17.536
"David Copperfield's
History of Magic"

00:07:17.536 --> 00:07:19.038
is available now.

